o well for Jakob  and the caronian but another colonial  opportunity presented itself in 1651  Gambia was taking an active role in the  transatlantic slave trade courland was  granted a small colony in Gambia Bites  king and returned for annual payments  and after this Jakob was sure to push  the idea of maintaining good relations  with the natives  Jakob gave colonizing Tobago one last  try in 1654 but this time he took the  lessons he learned over the previous  decade in half and utilized them  properly first of all he sent over 120  soldiers to Tobago to protect the colony  from both the natives in any foreign  powers second he recruited settlers from  many other nations as well as courland  itself and third he made sure the  efforts were made to accommodate the  natives and they were given legal rights  there the colony was settled by thousand  of people and was renamed new corland  with its capital being Jakob stat the  caronian approaches success is proved by  the fact that within four years the  colony's populations has at twenty five  thousand people with about five thousand  of those being caronian x' the rest had  pledged their loyalty to Jakob and core  London of the twenty five thousand  people who lived there roughly 13,000  were slaves from core lands can be in  colony and so it seemed that the  caronian approach to colonization had  worked which raises the question why  wasn't there a continuous Latvian  speaking population in the Caribbean  then well in 1656 Courland as part of  the numerous ongoing swedish polish wars  was invaded and in 1658 Jakob was  captured whilst he was imprisoned the  Dutch enticed the caronia garrison to  revolt and so Jakob then signed the  colony over to them in 1664 now no  longer able to project power overseas  Colin ceded his Gambian colony to  England and thus the shortly of Latvian  attempt to colonialism was over I hope  you enjoyed this episode and thank you  for watching with extra thanks to these  patrons you can 